                      <td><font class="news"><a href="modules.php?name=News&amp;new_topic=7"><img src="images/topics/officialnews.gif" alt="Official EQII News" title="Official EQII News" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>Here is a new feature that will be heading to the test servers in a couple of days.  Click on Read More at the bottom of the news post to view the rest of this feature and click <a href="http://www.eq2servers.com/modules.php?name=News&file=article&sid=70"><b>here</b></a> to visit out forums to discuss this new feature.

<P><b>Scott:</b> One of our goals with EverQuest II is to make it as easy as possible to group up with the people you want to be playing with. Over the past few weeks, we've been working on a way to let friends adventure with friends, no matter what level anyone is.

<P>With that goal in mind, we're pleased to announce EverQuest II's new Mentoring system.

 

<P>What is Mentoring?

<P>The idea behind Mentoring is a straightforward one. It should mirror the analogy of a dedicated teacher offering valuable lessons to an eager student.


